From 95b8bb994888ef63d90cfbd3ab775196b82d2205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Show mute state and disappearing-messages timer in the
 personal chat info

Both come from data the client already holds, so nothing is asked of the
server and nothing in WPPConnect or client/api_patches changes:

- Notifications: the client's own _muted_chats map (kept in step with
  WhatsApp's muteExpiration on every chat list sync), read with the same
  rule as is_chat_muted: -1 is muted for good, a future expiry is muted
  until then, the other JID form (phone <-> @lid) is honoured.
- Disappearing messages: the ephemeralDuration wa-js puts on the chat in
  the list-chats snapshot (24 hours, 7 days, 90 days, off). It is only as
  fresh as that snapshot.

A missing value never turns into "not muted" or "off": with no data the
line is simply not shown. The logic is in core/chat_settings.py and the
dialog gets a single call.
